input:
Given that

\begin{align*}
\frac{1}{x}+\frac{1}{y}&=3,\\
xy+x+y&=4,
\end{align*}

compute $x^2y+xy^2$.

How many points of intersection are there between the graphs of the following equations: \begin{align*}
y &=|2x + 5|, \\
y &= -|3x - 2|
\end{align*}

Find $2^x$ if

\begin{align*}
2^x+3^y&=5,\\
2^{x+2}+3^{y+1} &=18.
\end{align*}

